"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    raw = sys.stdin.read()\n    tokens = raw.split()\n    if not tokens:\n        return\n    target = int(tokens[0])\n    size = target + 2\n    ways = [0] * size\n    ways[target] = 1\n    ways[target + 1] = 1\n    stair = target - 1\n    while stair >= 0:\n        a = ways[stair + 1]\n        b = ways[stair + 2]\n        ways[stair] = a + b\n        stair -= 1\n    print(ways[0])\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    solve()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"ways fills in from the top of the staircase down to the bottom. The two base cells start at 1, and each earlier cell reads the two cells one and two steps ahead of it and adds them, so both values it needs are always ready by the time it is computed.",
